<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Harbor Storage</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#091827;color:#dbeafe;font:16px system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:56px 24px}h1{font-size:42px;margin:0}p{color:#93a4b8;line-height:1.6}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:32px 0}.stat,.panel{padding:22px;background:#10263a;border:1px solid #24445f;border-radius:12px}.stat b{display:block;font-size:28px;color:#67e8f9}.panel{max-width:720px}code{color:#67e8f9;word-break:break-word}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.panel{transition:border-color .2s}.panel:hover{border-color:#38bdf8}}</style></head><body><main><p>Harbor Storage / control room</p><h1>Your objects stay on your server.</h1><div class="grid"><div class="stat"><b>S3</b><span>Signature V4 API</span></div><div class="stat"><b>100 MB</b><span>Default object ceiling</span></div><div class="stat"><b>30 days</b><span>Trash retention</span></div></div><section class="panel"><h2>Create the first credential</h2><p>Run this once from the cPanel terminal. Store the secret immediately; it is only displayed once.</p><code>php artisan object-store:key --scope=read --scope=write --scope=delete</code><p>Configure clients with path-style addressing and the endpoint <code>/s3</code>.</p></section></main></body></html>
